@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: Zendesk Ticket Routing when Organization is unset
	Testing Zendesk tickets that have their organization removed.

Teardown:
	* I wait for "30" seconds
	* I teardown the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "osbadmin.admin@liferay.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| ZENOSBA |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken |
	| no-reply@zenosba.com.broken      |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Zen OSB Automotive |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View empty fields
	Zendesk tickets that have their organization removed should have their accountCode and organizationExternalId fields emptied

	Given I wait for "30" seconds
	And I log into the support homepage as "osbadmin.admin@liferay.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	And I create a project with the following values
	| Name         | Zen OSB Automotive |
	| Code         | ZENOSBA            |
	| Type         | Group              |
	| Industry     | Automotive         |
	| Tier         | Premier            |
	| Max Contacts | 10                 |
	| Address Line | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country      | United States      |
	| State        | California         |
	| City         | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip          | 91765              |
	| Region       | US                 |
	| Language     | English            |
	And I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Gold" to the project code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	When I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                     |
	| Organization     | Zen OSB Automotive               |
	| Language         | English                          |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)       | 
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	And I wait for "60" seconds
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product           | prd_liferay_portal_6_2                           |
	| Component         | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status     | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject           | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description       | Request Description                              |
	| Organization Name | Zen OSB Automotive                               |
	And I remove a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" from an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And I remove a user with the email address "no-reply@zenosba.com.broken" from an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	Then the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should have their accountCode and externalId fields empty